1. Difference between @SpringBootTest and @WebMvcTest?
..................................
@SpringBootTest                      	@WebMvcTest
Loads entire application	     Loads only Controller layer
Slower                           	Faster
Integration Testing	              Controller Unit Testing
Loads Service & Repository          	Uses mocked services
Starts full Spring context	       Starts MVC slice only

2. Why use MockMvc?
 ..................................
Tests REST APIs without starting an embedded server.
Faster execution.
Supports GET, POST, PUT, DELETE testing.

3. Difference between @ValueSource and @CsvSource?
..................................
@ValueSource	           @CsvSource
One parameter             	Multiple parameters
Single input type	                 Multiple values per test case
Simple data	                         Complex test scenarios

